From 3a777e8478de6ada57e032b0cd48285d670675f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:36:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: axisymmetrical generalised plane stress

The HenckyElasticity, GreenLagrangeElasticity and
SaintVenantKirchhoffElasticity test behaviours support the
AxisymmetricalGeneralisedPlaneStress hypothesis, whose axial component is
the second one (the third one in plane stress): one code block computes
the axial component for both hypotheses.

In both hypotheses, DisplacementGradientTest compares them with the
analytical solution (Cauchy and first Piola-Kirchhoff stresses, axial
strain or axial deformation gradient, tangent operator of the behaviour
written with the deformation gradient, with F and with H, axial
component shifted by the caller) and checks the initial value of the
axial deformation gradient. For the behaviours written in a strain
framework, it also compares the integration with F and with H for all
the stress measures and tangent operators, and the initialize functions
and post-processings. The in-plane strains of the analytical case are
now biaxial (the second in-plane stress was zero). The handling of the
axial component by the generic interface of TFEL in this hypothesis was
not tested before.
